[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise. They were
merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so nobody read
them. Read by tenant, by form and by what each body describes, they hold three problems. Each
now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other two need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} tickets={tickets} />

### `parser`: day-first dates read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first, so
any date with both parts at 12 or under comes back swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. App, email
and booking-v2 form reports. This is the bug #4471 describes, and the fix that is queued.

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the input the tenant's way,
day first. People do what the hint says and get a swapped date. Only form submissions on
booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix does not touch this: the form's hint, or how it reads, has to
change.

### `one-day`: dates move by one day

These are not swaps. The booking lands one day early, and the same meeting shows different days
in different time zones ("Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). That is
time-zone handling, not field order. The desk noted these reports but still counted them under the
parser.

## The table on #4471, for comparison

Built by `causes.ts`, which files the one-day moves under the parser by tenant and leaves `hint`
without a ticket of its own:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes on the desk

- Count unique report ids. The export pages overlap and repeat rows.
- Place a report by its tenant and form, then by its body. Intake's tag is a guess from the browser
  and disagrees with the tenant often.
- A subject line says what hurt, not why. Read the body before merging into a big ticket.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
